#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5384
#, kde-format
msgid "Compressor/Expander"
msgstr "Kompresor/razširjevalnik"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5386
#, kde-format
msgid "Compress or expand the audio’s dynamic range."
msgstr "Stisnite ali razširite dinamični obseg zvoka."

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5388
#, kde-format
msgid "Attacks"
msgstr "Vnihavanje"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5390 rc.cpp:5394
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"A list of times in seconds for each channel over which the instantaneous "
"level of the input signal is averaged to determine its volume. Attacks "
"refers to increase of volume and decays refers to decrease of volume. For "
"most situations, the attack time (response to the audio getting louder) "
"should be shorter than the decay time, because the human ear is more "
"sensitive to sudden loud audio than sudden soft audio. A typical value for "
"attack is 0.3 seconds and a typical value for decay is 0.8 seconds. If "
"specified number of attacks and decays is lower than number of channels, the "
"last set attack/decay will be used for all remaining channels."
msgstr ""
"Seznam časov v sekundah za vsak kanal, v katerem se povpreči trenutna raven "
"vhodnega signala, da se določi njegova glasnost. Napadi se nanašajo na "
"povečanje glasnosti, upadi pa na zmanjšanje glasnosti. V večini primerov "
"mora biti čas napada (odziv na glasnejši zvok) krajši od časa upada, ker je "
"človeško uho bolj občutljivo na nenaden glasen zvok kot na nenaden tišji "
"zvok. Tipična vrednost za napad je 0,3 sekunde, tipična vrednost za upad pa "
"0,8 sekunde. Če je določeno število napadov in upadov manjše od števila "
"kanalov, bo zadnji nastavljen napad/upad uporabljen za vse preostale kanale."

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5392
#, kde-format
msgid "Decays"
msgstr "Upadi"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5396
#, kde-format
msgid "Soft-Knee"
msgstr "Mehko koleno"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5398
#, kde-format
msgid "Set the curve radius in dB for all joints."
msgstr "Polmer krivulje nastavite v dB za vse spoje."

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5402
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"Set the additional gain in dB to be applied at all points on the transfer "
"function. This allows for easy adjustment of the overall gain."
msgstr ""
"Nastavite dodatno ojačitev v dB, ki se uporabi na vseh točkah prenosne "
"funkcije. To omogoča enostavno prilagajanje celotne ojačitve."

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5404
#, kde-format
msgid "Initial volume"
msgstr "Začetna glasnost"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5406
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"Set an initial volume, in dB, to be assumed for each channel when filtering "
"starts. This permits the user to supply a nominal level initially, so that, "
"for example, a very large gain is not applied to initial signal levels "
"before the companding has begun to operate. A typical value for audio which "
"is initially quiet is -90 dB."
msgstr ""
"Nastavite začetno glasnost v dB, ki se predvidi za vsak kanal ob začetku "
"filtriranja. To uporabniku omogoča, da na začetku zagotovi nominalno raven, "
"tako da se npr. zelo velika ojačitev ne uporabi za začetne ravni signala, "
"preden se začne izvajati postopek. Tipična vrednost za zvok, ki je na "
"začetku tih, je -90 dB."

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compensationdelay.xml
#: rc.cpp:5408
#, kde-format
msgid "Compensation Delay"
msgstr "Kompenzacijska zakasnitvena linija"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compensationdelay.xml
#: rc.cpp:5410
#, fuzzy, kde-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Compensation Delay Line is a metric based delay to compensate differing "
#| "positions of microphones or speakers.\n"
#| "For example, you have recorded guitar with two microphones placed in "
#| "different locations. Because the front of sound wave has fixed speed in "
#| "normal conditions, the phasing of microphones can vary and depends on "
#| "their location and interposition. The best sound mix can be achieved when "
#| "these microphones are in phase (synchronized). Note that a distance of "
#| "~30 cm between microphones makes one microphone capture the signal in "
#| "antiphase to the other microphone. That makes the final mix sound moody. "
#| "This filter helps to solve phasing problems by adding different delays to "
#| "each microphone track and make them synchronized.\n"
#| "\n"
#| "The best result can be reached when you take one track as base and "
#| "synchronize other tracks one by one with it. Remember that "
#| "synchronization/delay tolerance depends on sample rate, too. Higher "
#| "sample rates will give more tolerance. "
msgid ""
"Compensation Delay Line is a metric based delay to compensate differing "
"positions of microphones or speakers.\n"
"For example, you have recorded guitar with two microphones placed in "
"different locations. Because the front of sound wave has fixed speed in "
"normal conditions, the phasing of microphones can vary and depends on their "
"location and interposition. The best sound mix can be achieved when these "
"microphones are in phase (synchronized). Note that a distance of ~30 cm "
"between microphones makes one microphone capture the signal in antiphase to "
"the other microphone. That makes the final mix sound moody. This filter "
"helps to solve phasing problems by adding different delays to each "
"microphone track and make them synchronized.\n"
"\n"
"The best result can be reached when you take one track as base and "
"synchronize other tracks one by one with it. Remember that synchronization/"
"delay tolerance depends on sample rate, too. Higher sample rates will give "
"more tolerance."
msgstr ""
"Kompenzacijska linijska zakasnitev je zakasnitev, ki temelji na metriki, za "
"kompenzacijo različnih položajev mikrofonov ali zvočnikov.\n"
"Primer: posneli ste kitaro z dvema mikrofonoma, nameščenima na različnih "
"mestih. Ker ima sprednji del zvočnega vala v navadnih pogojih fiksno "
"hitrost, se lahko fazi mikrofonov razlikujeta in sta odvisni od njunega "
"mesta in medsebojne razdalje. Najboljšo zvočno mešanico lahko dosežemo, ko "
"so ti mikrofoni v fazi (sinhronizirani). Upoštevajte, da razdalja ~ 30 cm "
"med mikrofoni povzroči, da en mikrofon zajame signal v protifazi z drugim "
"mikrofonom. Zaradi tega končni miks zveni muhasto. Ta filter pomaga rešiti "
"težave s fazami tako, da vsaki stezi mikrofona doda različne zakasnitve in "
"jih sinhronizira.\n"
"\n"
"Najboljši rezultat lahko dosežete, če eno stezo vzamete kot osnovo in z njo "
"sinhronizirate druge steze eno za drugo. Ne pozabite, da je toleranca "
"sinhronizacije / zakasnitve odvisna tudi od mere vzorčenja. Višje mere "
"vzorčenja bodo nudile več tolerance. "

